# HARP IMU Bench Characterization (Step 1)

Standalone (no ROS) characterization of the cart heading IMUs, run on the cart Pi (`rpi4u`)
with the sensors in their final mounted positions. Purpose: prove a MEMS gyro fixes the
wheel-odometry heading problem before building it into the drive node and EKF.

**Status: Step 1 PASSED (2026-09-28).** Primary heading sensor: MPU-6050 (GY-521).

---

## 1. Why this step exists

Cart bring-up (see `HARP_Cart_Drive_BringUp_AsRun_Session_Record_v1`) measured wheel-odometry
heading error of about ±2.4% of rotation, **direction-dependent** (floor scrub: effective track
CW 441.9 mm vs CCW 421.1 mm). That is about 8.6° per 360° turn and cannot be removed with a
single calibration constant. A gyro's scale error is a fixed per-sensor constant, so it can.

## 2. Hardware and mounting

| Item | Detail |
|---|---|
| Sensors | GY-521 (MPU-6050) at I2C 0x68; Adafruit ICM-20948 at 0x69 (ADR jumper as shipped). HW-123 (MPU-6050) kept as spare |
| Bus | Pi I2C1, shared: pin 1 3.3 V, pin 3 SDA/GPIO2, pin 5 SCL/GPIO3, pin 6 GND. Both boards powered from 3.3 V |
| Pull-ups | Pi 1.8 kΩ ∥ GY-521 4.7 kΩ ∥ Adafruit 10 kΩ = 1.15 kΩ, 2.9 mA sink at 3.3 V (I2C limit 3 mA). 0 I2C errors across all runs |
| Location | Between the DROK buck and the Pi, about 100 mm from each; both at the same height; not on the drive centerline; each board with a different yaw orientation |
| Orientation | **Both boards Z-down** (accel: MPU az = −0.994 g, ICM az = −1.006 g). Heading rate (REP-103, CCW +) = **−gz** |
| Tilt | MPU 0.5°, ICM 2.8° (the ICM value may be partly accel zero-offset). Absorbed by in-situ scale calibration |
| Config | Gyro ±500 dps, accel ±4 g, ~100 Hz output data rate, DLPF config 3, polled at 100 Hz |

**Clock note:** the ICM-20948 internal clock can be off by up to ±9% without timebase
correction. All integration uses Pi `time.monotonic_ns()` stamps, never an assumed sample period.

## 3. Scripts

| Script | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `imu_log.py` | Dual-sensor raw logger. `--duration` (0 = until Ctrl-C), `--tag`, `--only mpu\|icm`. Writes `logs/<tag>_<stamp>.csv` (raw counts, scale factors in header, `err` column) |
| `analyze_soak.py` | Stationary soak: warm-up, bias tempco (linear fit), residual after T-compensation, Allan deviation (noise density with the √2 one-sided correction, ARW, bias instability), fusion gain and correlation |
| `analyze_spin.py` | Multi-turn spin: bias from the stationary ends, trapezoid integration on host timestamps, scale factor vs `--truth` (deg, CCW +) |

Raw CSVs are gitignored (`tools/imu_bench/logs/*.csv`, about 13 MB per 30 min soak) and live on
`rpi4u` only. Plots and this README are the committed record.

## 4. Results: 30 min cold soak (`soak_cold_20260927_195514`)

Pi powered off for at least 30 min beforehand, then logging started at boot. Sensors in final
position with the Pi and DROK running.

| Metric | MPU-6050 | ICM-20948 | Datasheet (MPU / ICM) |
|---|---|---|---|
| Die temperature rise | 1.74 °C | 1.29 °C | — |
| Bias span, 30 min | 0.0093 dps | 0.0383 dps | — |
| Bias settles (±0.01 dps) | 0.5 min | 16.5 min | — |
| Tempco (fit) | −0.0007 dps/°C (R² 0.02) | −0.026 dps/°C (R² 0.58) | ±0.16 / ±0.05 |
| Residual after T-compensation | 0.0021 dps rms | 0.0070 dps rms | — |
| Noise density | 0.0058 dps/√Hz | 0.0133 dps/√Hz | 0.005 / 0.015 |
| Bias instability | 4.9 °/h | 9.2 °/h | — |
| ZUPT stop for 0.01 dps bias | 0.17 s | 0.88 s | — |

- Measured noise matches the datasheets at 100 mm from the switching buck, so there is no
  detectable electrical pickup at this location.
- Fusion: σ ratio 3.42, correlation −0.25, optimal gain 1.15×. Below the fuse threshold
  (ratio < 1.5 and |ρ| < 0.3), so the pair is used as primary plus cross-check, not averaged.

## 5. Results: 10-turn scale calibration (on the cart, in situ)

Truth came from a protractor reading between a chassis edge and a floor tape line.
Sequence: ≥10 s still, spin via `tools/cart_bringup/spin.py`, ≥10 s still.

| Run (log) | Truth | MPU error | ICM error | ICM/MPU ratio |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| CCW 1 (`ccw10_20260928_102129`) | +3718.8° | −0.056% | +0.059% | 1.00115 |
| CW (`cw10_20260928_104443`) | −3721.0° | −0.202% | −0.159% | 1.00042 |
| CCW 2 (`ccw10_20260928_112929`) | +3718.0° | −0.310% | −0.255% | 1.00054 |
| **Mean** | | **−0.189%** | **−0.118%** | |
| Run-to-run std dev | | 0.127% | 0.161% | 0.04% |

**Direction symmetry (pass criterion < 0.2%):** MPU CCW average −0.183% vs CW −0.202%, a gap of
**0.019%**. ICM −0.098% vs −0.159%, a gap of **0.061%**. **Both pass.**

**Scatter source:** the two CCW runs had nearly equal truth (118.8° vs 118.0° past 10 turns), but
both gyros shifted about 10–12° together while their ratio held within 0.07%. That common-mode
signature points to protractor reading error at large angles (about ±5°), not the sensors.
Lesson: one protractor misread (89° vs 118°) produced a spurious +0.5% result. The truth-free
inter-sensor ratio is the check that caught it.

## 6. Decisions carried forward

| Decision | Basis |
|---|---|
| **MPU-6050 (GY-521) is the primary heading sensor** | 3.4× better bias residual, near-zero tempco, 0.5 min warm-up |
| **Scale correction k_MPU = 1.0019, k_ICM = 1.0012** | Pooled mean of 3 runs; 95% CI about ±0.3% (includes 1.000). Refine later against fiducials |
| **Bias estimated at every stop**, window ≥ 0.2 s | Measured ZUPT requirement (MPU 0.17 s) |
| **yaw_rate = −gz**; encode as `imu_link` roll = π in the URDF | Both boards Z-down; driver publishes raw sensor frame |
| **ICM-20948 as cross-check monitor** | Inter-sensor agreement about 0.1% of angle (about 0.4°/turn). Initial alarm about 2° per 360°, to be tuned in Step 3 |
| No magnetometer in fusion | Indoor, near motors and the 12 V trunk |

**Heading performance vs wheels:** about 0.1–0.7° per 360° turn (gyro), against 8.6° (wheels).
More than 10× improvement. Feasibility proven.

## 7. Open items

1. **Measure each board's x/y offset from the drive-wheel midpoint and its yaw rotation** for the URDF `imu_link` frames.
2. **Ambient-range soak:** the in-situ soak saw only a 1.3–1.7 °C rise. Repeat at a different room or ambient temperature to confirm the MPU's near-zero tempco holds.
3. **Accelerometer tilt (future stair use):** off-center mounting gives centripetal a = ω²r (about 0.04 g, about 2° false tilt at 112 °/s, r = 0.1 m). Compensate with ω²r, or gate tilt updates while |ω| is large.
4. **`analyze_spin.py` stillness flag** (1 dps peak) trips on the cart's start/stop rocking. Loosen it, or use windows ending before motion onset. Pre/post bias agreement is the real check.
5. Optional part-to-part check: swap the HW-123 in for the ICM and repeat the soak.

## 8. Next: Step 2 carry-in

Step 2 is the ROS 2 drive node (`src/harp_cart_drive`, runs on `rpi4u`) **without** the IMU:
`cmd_vel` in, `odom` out. It uses the bring-up parameters (wheel diameter 95.8 mm, track
430 mm, per-motor QPPS). **Acceptance:** reproduce the ±0.2% straight run through ROS 2.

Step 3 then fuses the MPU yaw rate in `robot_localization` and re-runs the spin test.
**Acceptance:** CW and CCW heading error each within about ±0.5% per turn (vs ±2.4% for wheels).

Workspace conventions (Step 0): one `zstair_ws` repo on every machine; per-host launch file in
`harp_bringup` (`rpi4u.launch.py`); machine-specific values in YAML; build per machine
(`colcon build --packages-up-to …`); `ROS_DOMAIN_ID=0`, `ROS_AUTOMATIC_DISCOVERY_RANGE=SUBNET`,
Cyclone DDS on all machines.